1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:14,306
In this video you will learn two simple tools in NTSOne: Contributions, to track money
that a group collects, and Wish lists, to plan what you want to get. The names and
amounts shown are sample data.

2
00:00:14,906 --> 00:00:34,343
Open Contributions and choose New contribution. Give it a name and say what the money
is for. Choose Monthly, for dues that people pay every month, or One time. Add the
columns you want to keep for each contributor, such as their name and phone number,
and the expected monthly amount.

3
00:00:34,943 --> 00:00:45,760
Each contribution shows the money collected, the money taken out, and the money still
held. The Overview tab also shows the totals year by year and who is behind.

4
00:00:46,360 --> 00:01:07,976
The Monthly tracker has a row for every contributor and a column for every month. Paid
months are green, a month paid less than expected is orange, and a month not paid is
red. Click a month to record a payment. Once a month has passed, a recorded payment is
locked, but months that were never filled in can still be filled in later.

5
00:01:08,576 --> 00:01:26,022
The Contributors tab is where you add and edit the people. Money taken records every
amount the group takes out, with a note saying why, so the balance held is always
clear. History keeps a record of every change, and you can export any table to Excel
or CSV.

6
00:01:26,622 --> 00:01:42,089
Wish lists are private lists of things you want to buy or have. Choose New wish list,
give it a name, and optionally a budget and a target date. Then choose Add items, and
add what you wish for, one by one or many at once.

7
00:01:42,689 --> 00:02:02,179
Type each item with an optional quantity and price each, or paste a whole list. The
priority and category you choose apply to all the items you add together. You can edit
an item later to add more details. You can search the list, filter it by priority or
category, and sort it.

8
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:21,996
When you get something, press Got it. Enter the total price you paid, the date you got
it, and where it came from, with an optional note. It moves to the Gotten tab, which
shows how much you saved compared with the price you expected, and the progress bar
shows how much of your budget is spent.

9
00:02:22,596 --> 00:02:36,973
The Summary tab shows your budget, and your items by category, by month and by
priority. The Activity tab is a record that cannot be changed. Nothing is ever
deleted: removed items stay in the records.

10
00:02:37,573 --> 00:02:54,874
You can share a list with family or friends. Choose Invite someone, and they get their
own private link and QR code. You decide whether they can only look, or also add and
change items. They do not need an account, and they can only see that one list.

11
00:02:55,474 --> 00:03:02,432
That is how you use contributions and wish lists in NTSOne. Use this video as your
guide.
